{title: The First Noel}
{key: D}
{time: 3/4}
{capo: 2}

The [D]first No[A7]el the [D]angel did [G]say
Was to [D]certain poor [G]shepherds in [A7]fields as they [D]lay;
In [D]fields where [A7]they lay [D]keeping their [G]sheep,
On a [D]cold winter's [G]night [A7]that was so [D]deep.

{label: Chorus}
No[D]el, No[A7]el, No[D]el, No[G]el,
[D]Born is the [G]King [A7]of [D]Israel.

They [D]looked [A7]up and [D]saw a [G]star
Shining [D]in the [G]east, be[A7]yond them [D]far;
And [D]to the [A7]earth it [D]gave great [G]light,
And [D]so it con[G]tinued both [A7]day and [D]night.

{label: Chorus}
No[D]el, No[A7]el, No[D]el, No[G]el,
[D]Born is the [G]King [A7]of [D]Israel.

Then [D]entered [A7]in those [D]wise men [G]three,
Full [D]reverent[G]ly up[A7]on their [D]knee,
And [D]offered [A7]there, in [D]His pres[G]ence,
Their [D]gold and [G]myrrh [A7]and frankin[D]cense.

{label: Chorus}
No[D]el, No[A7]el, No[D]el, No[G]el,
[D]Born is the [G]King [A7]of [D]Israel.
